%% Lifecycle of one private endpoint connection - the four Azure states plus the two operational states that decide whether traffic actually flows
%% Source: Microsoft Learn - What is a private endpoint (connection status Pending, Approved, Rejected, Disconnected; approval action Microsoft.Provider/resource_type/privateEndpointConnectionsApproval/action); codex/runbook-private-endpoint-name-resolution-and-reachability.md classes 2, 3 and 5
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB

  state "Not created - the account is reachable on its public endpoint only" as Absent
  state "Pending - created by an identity without privateEndpointConnectionsApproval on the target" as Pending
  state "Rejected - the resource owner declined. No traffic, ever" as Rejected
  state "Approved - the platform will carry traffic to the private-link resource" as Approved
  state "Approved but unresolvable - the NIC holds the IP, nothing answers the name with it" as Unresolvable
  state "Approved and serving - clients resolve to the NIC IP and reach it" as Serving
  state "Disconnected - the resource owner removed the connection. The endpoint is now informative and should be deleted" as Disconnected

  [*] --> Absent
  Absent --> Approved : created by an owner of the storage account or Storage Sync Service, auto-approved
  Absent --> Pending : created cross-subscription or by a network team without rights on the target
  Pending --> Approved : approve on the target resource Private endpoint connections blade
  Pending --> Rejected : owner declines
  Rejected --> [*] : delete and recreate with an authorised identity
  Approved --> Unresolvable : no DNS zone group, or a duplicate privatelink zone linked to the same VNet answers NXDOMAIN
  Unresolvable --> Serving : attach the DNS zone group to the central zone, add the Infoblox forwarder, Clear-DnsClientCache
  Approved --> Serving : DNS zone group writes the A record and the Infoblox forwarder is in place
  Serving --> Unresolvable : endpoint recreated with a new IP while a hand-made A record or hosts entry still points at the old one
  Serving --> Disconnected : connection deleted on the target resource
  Disconnected --> [*] : delete the orphaned endpoint and its IPAM reservation

  note right of Pending
    az network private-endpoint show
    query privateLinkServiceConnections[0]
    privateLinkServiceConnectionState.status
    Assessor rule NET-03 fires here
  end note

  note right of Unresolvable
    This is the dangerous state.
    Nothing is broken until the storage
    firewall goes to Deny - then every
    client fails at once with 403.
    Never lock down from this state.
  end note

  note right of Serving
    Gate - Resolve-DnsName returns the
    CNAME to the privatelink name and a
    10.x A record on EVERY Contoso server,
    and Test-NetConnection on 445 and 443
    is True. Only then set defaultAction Deny.
  end note
